WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.292
She asked the agent to inspect a capability change.

00:00:03.292 --> 00:00:05.201
It queued publication instead.

00:00:05.201 --> 00:00:06.518
The command is ready.

00:00:06.518 --> 00:00:08.032
The agent has the tools.

00:00:08.032 --> 00:00:11.258
But the organization never authorized that change.

00:00:11.258 --> 00:00:13.891
What should happen before anything runs?.

00:00:14.891 --> 00:00:17.582
Meet the intended SideFX experience.

00:00:17.582 --> 00:00:18.504
One engineer.

00:00:18.504 --> 00:00:19.965
One proposed change.

00:00:19.965 --> 00:00:22.425
One action waiting at a boundary.

00:00:22.425 --> 00:00:30.344
The interlock connects the requested operation to the exact capability, session, and admitted authority.

00:00:30.344 --> 00:00:34.342
Execution stays pending while that decision is made.

00:00:35.342 --> 00:00:37.550
She needs the inspection today.

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:40.199
Stopping everything leaves her stuck.

00:00:40.199 --> 00:00:43.511
Letting everything through surrenders control.

00:00:43.511 --> 00:00:53.593
A useful boundary tells the agent what it may do next, so the engineer can keep moving without silently approving more than she intended.

00:00:54.593 --> 00:00:56.751
First, open the current capsule.

00:00:56.751 --> 00:01:00.579
Its stored adjudication expression checks the tool name.

00:01:00.579 --> 00:01:03.364
Dangerous-tool returns OPERATOR REQUIRED.

00:01:03.364 --> 00:01:05.870
The alternative branch returns ALLOW.

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:10.394
Its activation and certification expressions return status fields.

00:01:10.394 --> 00:01:13.179
These are inspectable decision semantics.

00:01:13.179 --> 00:01:17.564
They do not yet demonstrate live interception of a tool action.

00:01:18.564 --> 00:01:20.950
Now project the stronger target.

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:25.338
An attempted effect reaches the interlock before dispatch.

00:01:25.338 --> 00:01:31.264
Resolve the capability, authority, requested mechanic, and permitted boundary.

00:01:31.264 --> 00:01:33.266
PERMIT can reach execution.

00:01:33.266 --> 00:01:35.960
OPERATOR REQUIRED waits for a human.

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:40.655
DENY or RESOLVE returns the reason and the next legal action.

00:01:41.655 --> 00:01:45.551
The gap is the connection between deciding and enforcing.

00:01:45.551 --> 00:01:48.891
A returned label cannot stop a command by itself.

00:01:48.891 --> 00:01:59.328
The target operating environment must intercept the covered action, verify the exact session and authority, and dispatch only the permitted capability.

00:01:59.328 --> 00:02:02.946
The unfinished boundary marks the work that remains.

00:02:03.946 --> 00:02:07.429
In our target simulation, publication stays pending.

00:02:07.429 --> 00:02:12.208
The interlock resolves the authorized next step: inspect the candidate.

00:02:12.208 --> 00:02:15.896
That inspection receives PERMIT and returns its report.

00:02:15.896 --> 00:02:20.403
Missing authority or coverage produces a hold with an exact reason.

00:02:20.403 --> 00:02:25.797
A consequential operation needing an operator waits for that separate decision.

00:02:26.797 --> 00:02:36.396
Closure requires the same live session to deny an unmanaged probe and permit a declared read-only probe, with exact identity and coverage evidence.

00:02:36.396 --> 00:02:40.538
A receipt must connect the request, decision, and actual effect.

00:02:40.538 --> 00:02:43.957
The reference simulation teaches those relationships.

00:02:43.957 --> 00:02:47.968
It does not claim the current platform already enforces them.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:53.894
In the intended outcome, the engineer has the inspection she asked for.

00:02:53.894 --> 00:02:58.608
Publication remains pending until its own authority and proof close.

00:02:58.608 --> 00:03:01.353
Today we can inspect decision semantics.

00:03:01.353 --> 00:03:04.730
The future adds live interception before effects.

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:10.219
That gap is the engineering runway: it tells us exactly what must become real.

00:03:11.219 --> 00:03:14.298
Stopping an unauthorized action is useful.

00:03:14.298 --> 00:03:23.761
But what happens when humans cannot clearly see what the agent is trying to change? Next: Reveal and Refine Capability Meaning.

00:03:23.761 --> 00:03:30.670
The Future of Agentic Engineering continues with making meaning visible enough to challenge.
